# Verify Before Asking

Never ask the user to commit, review, ship, or choose next work until the change is verified as working.

## Required before any ask

1. **Reproduce the user path** — open the real URL/page (or run the real command) that the change affects.
2. **Check the critical UX** — for UI: layout, click targets, LCP/hero, console errors; for scripts: exit code + expected output.
3. **Fix failures first** — if anything looks broken, incomplete, or “kinda works”, keep fixing. Do not hand off.
4. **Only then ask** — commit / PR / “làm tiếp P1?” only after verification passes.

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ “Em tối ưu xong, anh commit không?”  (chưa mở trang kiểm tra kỹ)
❌ “Có vẻ ổn, anh xem giúp…”           (agent chưa tự verify)
✅ Open page → click Play / rails / console → fix issues → then report + ask
```

## Bar for “ổn”

- Happy path works without console errors that block use
- No obvious layout collapse, unclickable CTAs, or missing assets on the changed surface
- Regressions on the same page type are checked (not only one file in isolation)
